code: 0
--- stdout
gh dojo moves issues through a GitHub Projects board with process verbs
defined in .github/dojo.toml, so agents never deal with field or option IDs.

Usage:
  gh dojo [flags]
  gh dojo [command]

Process verbs (from .github/dojo.toml):
  note        You want to leave a note without moving the issue

Additional Commands:
  block       Mark an issue blocked by other issues, without changing its status
  comment     Comment on an issue without changing its status
  describe    Learn this project's process: verbs, statuses and exit codes in a few lines
  doctor      Find what is broken in the setup: config, token scope, board, repositories
  help        Help about any command
  init        Write .github/dojo.toml for a board and check it against the board
  list        See what is on the board: one line per open issue, grouped by status
  new         Create an issue with labels, on the board, in the initial status
  show        Read issues before working on them: board status, blockers, history, description, comments
  unblock     Remove blocked-by links of an issue, without changing its status

Lifecycle (from → to):
  note        any status → status unchanged

Exit codes:
  0  everything applied: go on
  1  bad arguments or config: fix them as the error says
  2  a process check refused: don't work around it; ask the user
  3  issue or board not found: check the number (gh dojo list) or board.owner/project in .github/dojo.toml
  4  network, rate limit or auth: retry later, or gh auth refresh -s project
  5  partially applied: re-run the same command; it finishes the rest

Flags:
  -h, --help                help for gh dojo
  -q, --jq expression       filter the JSON with a jq expression (implies --json)
      --json                print the result as JSON (schema_version 1), errors too
  -t, --template template   format the JSON with a Go template (implies --json)
  -v, --version             version for gh dojo

Use "gh dojo [command] --help" for more information about a command.
